<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef lower on moderate demand and moderate to heavy offerings.  Select and Choice rib and loin cuts weak, while chuck and round cuts lower.  Beef trimmings generally steady on light to moderate demand and offerings. -USDA</p>
<p>-----</p>
<p>324 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 42 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>26 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     105.45	105.20	100.05	 99.73</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.96	 -0.65	 -1.16	 -0.95</p>
<p>Rib	  157.67	158.33	146.98	147.37</p>
<p>Chuck	 73.28	 70.44	 73.33	 70.74</p>
<p>Round	 91.45	 91.45	 87.59	 87.59</p>
<p>Loin	 167.81	170.26	151.90	153.84</p>
<p>Brisket     60.96	 60.96	 60.72	 60.72</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  71.41	 71.32	 71.69	 71.49</p>
<p>Flank	 60.79	 60.79	 60.53	 60.53</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
